# Leaks that belong to the font stack, so a sweep's output is only about us.
#
# A storm feeds the interface names and descriptions holding characters the
# default font has no glyph for. Drawing one makes Qt ask fontconfig for a
# fallback, and FcFontMatch/FcFontRenderPrepare keep the pattern they build.
# fontconfig is not instrumented here, so LeakSanitizer sees the allocation
# and not what holds it.
#
# It is worth being exact about why this is not ours: every frame between the
# allocation and QQuickTextMetrics::width() is inside libfontconfig or
# QFontEngineMultiFontConfig, and the same 1867 bytes in 42 allocations are
# reported on ten different seeds -- one fallback lookup, not a growing
# structure. The larger reports vary with the state of the font cache in
# XDG_CACHE_HOME, which is the same thing seen while the cache is cold.
#
# Anything else the check reports is ours to look at.
leak:libfontconfig
leak:FcFontMatch
leak:FcFontRenderPrepare
leak:QFontEngineMultiFontConfig
